             evaluated under an erratum-affected rule version?"). After
             CompositionValidator, EventTopology and DataFootprint — it seeds
             versions from all three exported manifests — and after
             ConfigValidatorAggregator (stamps a ValidatorOutcome run). Pure:
             registers nothing, decorates nothing. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionRuleVersioning.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 438 — authorization-surface manifest: every externally
             reachable thing a component contributes (route prefixes + exact
             route overrides under their Phase 66 admit sets, remoting API
             record fields through the Phase 69d classifier, AI-drivable tools,
             OnEvent job handlers) with its resolved default-deny
             classification — explicit requirement / inherited default-deny /
             anonymous-reachable. Plus the Phase 113 ActionPolicy resolution
             over the floor entries, and a severity-bearing id-keyed diff for
             the Phase 287 golden-file gate. After ServerApp (reads
             ServerModule) and Remoting\Auth.fs (reads the dispatcher's own
             AuthClassifier, so the manifest cannot drift from what is
             enforced); beside EventTopology / DataFootprint, the sibling
             derived lenses. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\AuthorizationSurface.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 627.E in-handler gate declarations for the platform-tier
             API records (JobApi / ModelExecutionApi / IModuleQueryBusApi).
             After AuthorizationSurface.fs, which declares the record they
             are expressed in. IFormApi's live in ToolUp.Forms.Server,
             beside its own handler. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\PlatformInHandlerGates.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 288 — component provenance: which package/assembly+version
             a composed companion came from, keyed by the same ComponentId the
             manifest carries (id-join, no manifest-shape change). After
             ServerApp (walks the composed companion set). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ComponentProvenance.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 588 — host-envelope descriptor: what THIS deployment offers
             a module — composed capability layers, every companion slot marked
             filled or open, each composed module's Phase 581 ModuleSurface, the
             config-knob schemas with the values this deployment resolved, the
             occupied route prefixes, and the platform build — plus canonical
             JSON + a SHA-256 stamp so an external authoring tool pins a
             snapshot and detects staleness. After ServerApp / CompositionManifest
             (the composed instance it projects), ComposableSurface.fs (the slot
             + knob universe it joins against), ModuleSurface.fs (the per-module
             surfaces it aggregates) and ComponentProvenance.fs (the platform
             version). Pure — registers nothing, decorates nothing (GP 11/13). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\HostEnvelope.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 290 — component health rollup: IHealthCheck results keyed by
             ComponentId into a per-component rollup (+ an Unkeyed bucket).
             After ServerApp (reads app.HealthChecks). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ComponentHealthRollup.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 291 — component lifecycle ordering: a declarative
             init-before partial order over ComponentIds + a stable
             topological init/dispose driver (dispose = reverse); a cycle is
             rejected at compose. Standalone (ComponentId only). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ComponentLifecycle.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 301 — live composition hot-swap: swap a declared companion
             impl on a running app by ComponentId, driven by the Phase 291
             lifecycle order (init new, atomic re-point, dispose old), atomic
             with rollback. Opt-in (HotSwapMode, default off). After
             ComponentLifecycle. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionHotSwap.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 284 — declarative composition descriptor: the serializable
             inverse of the Phase 280 manifest (component selection by
             ComponentId + ServerConfig) + RegistrationCatalogue +
             CompositionDescriptor.ofManifest / ServerApp.ofManifest. After
             ServerApp (folds addModule / with* builders). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionDescriptor.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 292 — descriptor schema-version + forward migration: an
             older CompositionDescriptor migrates to the current shape before
             ServerApp.ofManifest composes it; a too-new version fails
             readably. Hosts the versioned ServerApp.ofManifest (runs migrate
             first). After CompositionDescriptor.fs. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionDescriptorVersion.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 302 — per-tenant composition presets: resolve a tenant to a
             base preset descriptor + per-tenant hole bindings + per-tenant
             component config (Phase 289), composed via ofManifest;
             scope-isolated by construction. After CompositionDescriptor.fs
             (holes/apply) + ComponentConfigResolver.fs (Phase 289). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\TenantCompositionPreset.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 436 — null-composition dry-run harness: rebind every
             companion slot to the in-process default the slot already
             declares (derived from the Phase 293 reflected slot set — leaving
             a slot None IS selecting its default), rebuild through the Phase
             284 / 292 versioned ofManifest, run the Phase 281 / 294
             structural-class well-formedness rules, drive the Phase 291
             init/dispose order, and return a typed DryRunReport — zero
             external services, defects as findings rather than exceptions.
             Plus the Expecto-shaped (Expecto-free) DryRun.shouldCompose
             affordance for consumer suites + worked-example verification.
             After
             CompositionDescriptorVersion.fs (the versioned build path it
             drives), ComposableSurface.fs (the slot universe it null-binds),
             ComponentLifecycle.fs and CompositionValidator.fs. Nothing
             registers into DI — a consumer that never calls it composes
             byte-for-byte what it did before (GP 11 / GP 13). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionDryRun.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 435 — cross-version composition upgrade planner: given this
             instance's Phase 280 manifest + Phase 288 provenance and the Phase
             293 ComposableSurface of a NEWER version set (data, so no new
             binaries need loading), compute a typed CompositionUpgradePlan —
             which composed slots' contracts widened / changed / vanished, which
             Phase 292 descriptor schema hops the jump crosses in what order,
             and the convention-derived docs/migrations/<slug>.md pointer per
             step. Phase 286's structural diff applied across versions rather
             than across instances: both sides' slots are projected into the
             ComponentEntry shape (contract fingerprinted into Impl) so
             CompositionDiff.diff does the id-keyed pairing. After
             CompositionDiff.fs, ComposableSurface.fs, ComponentProvenance.fs,
             CompositionDescriptorVersion.fs (its migration-error rendering) and
             CompositionDryRun.fs (its slotInterface parser). Pure — nothing
             registers into DI, nothing runs at compose (GP 11 / GP 13). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\CompositionUpgradePlan.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 675 — the cumulative privacy-budget ledger, MOVED here
             from the federation companion (it was
             InterPlatform/Server/PrivacyBudgetLedger.fs, Phase 190). Two
             tiers now meter against it — the clean-room gate and the
             grounding tier's declassification routines — and a second
             implementation of a privacy control is how a path that
             enforces slightly less appears, so the seam sits at the layer
             both already depend on rather than minting a companion ->
             companion package edge (GP 1). Appended last: it needs
             IConditionalBlobStorage (Core) and the FableConverters set
             (Server/Remoting/Json/), and nothing above it needs it. -->
        <Compile Include="Server\PrivacyBudgetLedger.fs" />
        <!-- Phase 723 — the scope-enumeration seam (IScopeEnumerator + its
             ITeamStore-backed default) and the converged restart-recovery
             sweep (IIngestionRecoverySurface + IngestionRecoverySweep) the
             RAG and KnowledgeBase companions now share. After
             Teams\TeamManagement.fs (the default adapts ITeamStore.ListTeams
             rather than adding a member to it) and IngestionStatusStore.fs
             (the RAG-side surface adapter wraps IIngestionStatusStore).
             Nothing here registers into DI and nothing runs at compose — a
             deployment that composes no enumerator and no sweep is
             byte-for-byte unchanged (GP 11 / GP 13). -->
        <Compile Include="Server\ScopeEnumeration.fs" />
    </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Giraffe" />
    <!-- 0.4.4 — ToolUp.Remoting.{Json,Server,Giraffe,AspNetCore}
         PackageReferences dropped; source folded under Server/Remoting/
         per the Compile block above. Microsoft.IO.RecyclableMemoryStream
         was a transitive dep of ToolUp.Remoting.Server / Giraffe /
         AspNetCore — now declared explicitly. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.IO.RecyclableMemoryStream" />
    <!-- Phase 30a — Ed25519 signing / verification for
         IArtifactSigner / IArtifactVerifier defaults. MIT-licensed
         (GP 2 — no paid deps). Version pinned centrally in
         Directory.Packages.props. -->
    <PackageReference Include="BouncyCastle.Cryptography" />
    <!-- 0.4.4 — explicit FSharp.Core PackageReference. Pre-fold, the
         transitively-resolved FSharp.Core was 10.1.300 (Directory.Packages.props
         pins). Post-fold, one of the dropped ToolUp.Remoting.* packages
         no longer floors FSharp.Core, and NuGet picks 6.0.0 from a
         lower dep — which lacks the `objnull` type the F# 10 compiler
         emits. Explicit reference forces the centrally-pinned version
         back into scope. -->
    <PackageReference Include="FSharp.Core" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
